Z||000000||firstfiero||05-02-2001||12:15 AM||||     Okay here's one more dumb question. Seems that when they refilled my coolant after my little problem over the weekend they didn't fill it with enough coolant. The car ran over 220 degrees today when I was sitting in traffic. When I was taking my sunroof out of the front I took notice that the coolant was far below add. Do I fill it in the front at the over flow or at the enging? I don't want to get air caught in the system again so how do you burp it? Thanks||||reg||7
Z||000001||Oreif||05-02-2001||12:19 AM||||First, Park the car on a driveway nose down.<BR>(Or in a garage raise the rear of the car a bit)Then when the car is COOL, remove rear cap and thermostat, SLOWLY open the radiator cap in front. If there is air in it, it will hiss. Close cap once coolant starts to leak. Fill from back then re-install thermostat and cap. Fill overflow reservoir to proper level.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-02-2001).]||||reg||1
